  "notes": "{虚脱|きょだつ} describes a profound state of depletion, both physical and psychological.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {虚脱|きょだつ}{状態|じょうたい}: state of prostration\n- {虚脱感|きょだつかん}: feeling of exhaustion\n- {虚脱|きょだつ}する: to become prostrate\n\nMEDICAL CONTEXT:\nIn medical terminology, {虚脱|きょだつ} can refer to circulatory collapse or shock.\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {疲労|ひろう}: fatigue (more general)\n- {脱力|だつりょく}: loss of strength\n- ぐったり: exhausted, limp (onomatopoeia)",
